<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermann IV, Margrave of Baden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1135–<a href="/years/1190">1190</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermann IV was Margrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> from 1160 until his death in 1190, a supporter of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> in his Italian wars. Before he left on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>, his lands were divided, his son Henry receiving the castle of Hachberg and founding the Hachberg line. He died during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> in 1190.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hermann-iv-margrave-of-baden.jpg" alt="Hermann IV, Margrave of Baden" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Baden.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
